      "id": "724e45ef-b857-40a2-8bab-14bde85cf895",
      "name": "Extract Transcript Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.5,
      "position": [
        1184,
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Podcast: {{ $(\"Normalize Episode\").item.json.podcastName }}\nEpisode: {{ $(\"Normalize Episode\").item.json.episodeTitle }}\nDuration: {{ $json.durationMin }} minutes\nSpeakers detected: {{ $json.speakerCount }}\n\nTIMESTAMPED CHAPTER OUTLINE:\n{{ $json.chapterOutline }}\n\nFULL TRANSCRIPT:\n{{ $json.transcript }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are a senior podcast producer writing show materials that will be published without further editing.\n\nRules:\n- Work only from the transcript. Never invent facts, names, statistics, or resources that are not stated.\n- If the transcript does not mention any resources or action items, return an empty array rather than fabricating entries.\n- summary_250 must be flowing prose of 240-260 words, written for a listener deciding whether to press play. No bullet points, no meta-commentary such as in this episode.\n- executive_summary must be exactly 5 entries, each a complete sentence carrying a distinct substantive insight. Not topic labels.\n- show_notes must be markdown using the supplied chapter timestamps in MM:SS format, one bolded timestamp per section followed by 1-2 sentences. Only use timestamps present in the chapter outline.\n- key_topics: 4-8 short noun phrases suitable as database tags. Lowercase unless a proper noun.\n- resources_mentioned: books, tools, people, companies, or URLs explicitly referenced. Include enough context to identify each one.\n- action_items: concrete things a listener could do, phrased as imperatives.\n- key_takeaways: the durable lessons, distinct from the action items."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "id": "539d2ab9-a7db-4abf-a692-45ee193fd111",
      "name": "Generate Summaries and Show Notes",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        1408,
        112
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-5.4",
          "cachedResultName": "gpt-5.4"
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.7,
          "timeout": 180000,
          "maxRetries": 3
        }
      },
      "id": "c0f2f877-efee-4482-b0c7-8dfa03af9460",
      "name": "GPT 5.4 Content Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1408,
        640
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "OpenAi account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\"summary_250\":\"A 250 word prose summary of the episode.\",\"executive_summary\":[\"Point one\",\"Point two\",\"Point three\",\"Point four\",\"Point five\"],\"show_notes\":\"## Show Notes\",\"key_topics\":[\"automation\",\"scaling\"],\"resources_mentioned\":[\"Book: Example Title by Author\"],\"action_items\":[\"Audit your current workflow stack\"],\"key_takeaways\":[\"Automation compounds when documented\"]}"
      },
      "id": "5310e379-b968-47dc-84f4-21d64806e0b2",
      "name": "Summary Schema",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1568,
        640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Episode: {{ $(\"Normalize Episode\").item.json.episodeTitle }}\nEpisode link: {{ $(\"Normalize Episode\").item.json.episodeUrl }}\n\nEPISODE SUMMARY:\n{{ $(\"Generate Summaries and Show Notes\").item.json.output.summary_250 }}\n\nFULL TRANSCRIPT:\n{{ $(\"Extract Transcript Data\").item.json.transcript }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are a social media strategist. Each platform gets genuinely native content, never the same paragraph reworded. Quote only words actually spoken in the transcript.\n\nlinkedin_post: 1200-1800 characters. Open with a specific claim or counterintuitive observation from the episode, not a question. Short paragraphs separated by blank lines. Professional but not stiff. End with one open question. No more than 3 hashtags, on the final line.\n\nx_thread: 5-8 tweets, each under 280 characters including the numbering prefix. Tweet 1 is a standalone hook that earns the click without clickbait. Each later tweet delivers one concrete idea and can stand alone. Final tweet links to the episode. No hashtags except at most one in the last tweet.\n\nfacebook_post: 400-700 characters. Warmer and more conversational than LinkedIn. Story-led opening. One clear call to action. At most 2 emoji.\n\ninstagram_caption: 800-1500 characters. Hook in the first 125 characters because the rest is truncated in feed. Line breaks between thoughts. Ends with 8-12 relevant hashtags on their own lines.\n\npull_quotes: exactly 10 verbatim or lightly tightened quotes from the transcript, each 8-25 words, each strong enough to stand alone on a graphic. No speaker attribution inside the string. Prefer quotes containing a concrete image, number, or contrast."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "id": "1ce63c5d-cd6b-4184-9092-6fd11429a016",
      "name": "Generate Social Content",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        1696,
        112
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\"linkedin_post\":\"Long form LinkedIn post text.\",\"x_thread\":[\"1/ Hook tweet\",\"2/ Second tweet\"],\"facebook_post\":\"Conversational Facebook post.\",\"instagram_caption\":\"Caption with line breaks and hashtags.\",\"pull_quotes\":[\"Quote one\",\"Quote two\"]}"
      },
      "id": "f7bf0ce6-e5f1-42d2-9985-16474039b94a",
      "name": "Social Schema",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1728,
        640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Episode: {{ $(\"Normalize Episode\").item.json.episodeTitle }}\nOriginal description: {{ $(\"Normalize Episode\").item.json.episodeDescription }}\n\nSHOW NOTES:\n{{ $(\"Generate Summaries and Show Notes\").item.json.output.show_notes }}\n\nKEY TAKEAWAYS:\n{{ $(\"Generate Summaries and Show Notes\").item.json.output.key_takeaways }}\n\nFULL TRANSCRIPT:\n{{ $(\"Extract Transcript Data\").item.json.transcript }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are an SEO content strategist and long-form writer. Everything you produce must be grounded in the transcript.\n\nblog_title: 50-65 characters, front-loads the primary keyword, reads like a human wrote it.\n\nblog_draft: 900-1400 words of markdown. Structure: a 2-3 paragraph introduction that establishes the problem before naming the solution; 4-6 H2 sections with descriptive keyword-aware headings; short paragraphs of 2-4 sentences; at least one bulleted list where the content genuinely enumerates; a conclusion that resolves the introduction and points to the episode. Weave the primary keyword naturally into the intro, one H2, and the conclusion. Never keyword-stuff. Do not include the title as an H1, start at H2.\n\nprimary_keywords: 2-4 head terms this post could realistically rank for.\nsecondary_keywords: 5-10 long-tail supporting phrases.\ntags: 5-8 short taxonomy labels for a CMS.\n\nseo_title: an improved podcast episode title, 45-60 characters, more searchable than the original while staying faithful to the content.\nurl_slug: lowercase, hyphen-separated, 3-6 words, no stop words, no dates.\nmeta_description: 140-158 characters, includes the primary keyword, written as a promise rather than a summary.\nrecommended_categories: 2-3 standard podcast directory categories such as Technology, Business, Education, Health and Fitness."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "id": "95b689a9-a298-4008-9748-fee0b954dd00",
      "name": "Generate SEO and Blog",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        1984,
        112
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\"blog_title\":\"How Automation Compounds\",\"blog_draft\":\"## Introduction\",\"primary_keywords\":[\"workflow automation\"],\"secondary_keywords\":[\"n8n workflows\"],\"tags\":[\"automation\"],\"seo_title\":\"Scaling Automation Without Breaking It\",\"url_slug\":\"scaling-automation-without-breaking-it\",\"meta_description\":\"A 150 character description.\",\"recommended_categories\":[\"Technology\"]}"
      },
      "id": "50c8a932-67d6-4f7d-9e48-0272c2c750c6",
      "name": "SEO Schema",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1888,
        640
      ]
    },
    {
