    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Ingest\n\nRSS Feed Trigger is the production path - swap feedUrl for the client feed.\n\nManual Test Run plus Load Sample Episode gives an identical payload shape for testing without waiting for a new episode. The sample points at a real public AssemblyAI test file.",
        "width": 740,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "4e389b3a-093e-472b-9093-0e8a6fad08e9",
      "name": "Sticky Note bfb40789",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -928,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Transcribe (async)\n\nAssemblyAI takes the audio URL directly - no download, no binary, no file size ceiling.\n\nSubmit returns a job id, then Wait 45s and poll. Transcription State loops back on any status other than completed or error, so long episodes simply take more laps.\n\nspeaker_labels and auto_chapters are what give us diarization and the timestamped outline used for show notes.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 960,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "ce5f91f4-f75b-400f-a86a-1535af450469",
      "name": "Sticky Note d01834e6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -128,
        -48
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Generate\n\nThree separate chains rather than one mega-prompt: each has its own schema, its own failure surface, and can be re-run or swapped independently.\n\nAll three share one GPT-5.4 model node. Each uses a Structured Output Parser so downstream mapping never string-parses prose.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 960,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "ec873252-e8bf-4809-8dd5-a737a5b783aa",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1f270fa0",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        912,
        -128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Persist and notify\n\nNotion rich_text properties cap at 2000 chars, so short assets go in properties and long-form goes in page blocks, sliced across several paragraphs.\n\nTranscript is stored as an excerpt of about 7600 chars. See README for the block-append loop that removes this limit.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 740,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "1787c1c8-a8eb-4dcc-bd28-1369a2201ff0",
      "name": "Sticky Note dca47c19",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1920,
        -128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Failure paths\n\nEvery fallible node has retries and an error output. Failures converge here rather than killing the run silently.\n\n- Invalid RSS data goes to skipped and alerted, never transcribed\n- Submit, poll, or transcription error alerts with the execution id\n- Notion write failure alerts after 3 retries\n\nA separate Error Trigger workflow catches anything uncaught.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 1200,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "5202d6b6-390e-4d5e-a7e5-748e62e5bbd3",
      "name": "Sticky Note 65bd7a12",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        224,
        784
      ]
    }
